// PROMOTED from pending under dense (P8, 2026-08-13): AGREE on the
// dense engines — the class below is resolved by the dense-delivery
// rulings (design/dense_delivery.md); kept as a regression pin.
// 00's class inside a collection loop, where it multiplies: a callback's
// effect runs PER ELEMENT PER KERNEL INVOCATION while the loop's value
// channel correctly stays quiet.
//
//   timeout 25 graphix --no-fusion 04_hof_callback_effect_per_invocation.gx
//     @P1 @P2 @R(0, 2) @R(1, 2) @R(2, 2) @R(3, 2)
//   timeout 25 graphix 04_hof_callback_effect_per_invocation.gx
//     @P1 @P2 @R(0, 2) @P1 @P2 @R(1, 2) @P1 @P2 @R(2, 2) @P1 @P2 @R(3, 2)
//
// The source array is a CONSTANT: its slots fire once at init, so in the
// node-walk the callback body's `x` Ref produces once per position and
// the two prints happen exactly once. The value channel agrees perfectly
// in both modes (`@R` is identical, and the per-slot firing rule keeps
// the map result quiet), which is what makes this pure effect
// divergence — 4x here, unbounded in a long-running program.
//
// `#[native]` above the block used to pass, proving the loop and the
// DynCall inside the callback were genuinely compiled. STRICT FUSION
// (design/strict_fusion.md, 2026-09-01) node-walks the print DynCall,
// so the attribute is removed — the pin keeps guarding the effect
// cadence itself (identical on both engines).
//
// Fix: 00's part (1) for the value-gated builtins, plus 00's part (2)
// for the print family. Note the in-loop DynCall site passes site id 0
// (the shared key-0 bucket, `emit_dyncall_site_word` returns 0 at
// `loop_depth > 0`), so per-slot argument state is already the
// documented approximation there — a stale mask has to be computed per
// dispatch, from the per-iteration arg discs, not once per loop.
{
  let n = 0;
  select n { x if x < 3 => n <- (x ~ n) + 1, _ => never() };
  let a = [i64:1, i64:2];
  let r =
  { let m = array::map(a, |x| { println("@P[x]"); x * i64:2 }); (n, array::len(m)) };
  println("@R[r]");
  i64:0
}
